<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<chapter xml:id="ch-applications" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Applications of Spectral Theory</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>
      A process that moves probability around a finite set of states is described by a
      matrix, and its long-run behaviour is governed by the eigenvector belonging to
      eigenvalue one. This chapter follows that idea from a toy example about lunch
      through population models to the algorithm that ranked the early web.
    </p>
  </introduction>
  <xi:include href="applications/sec-markov-chains.ptx" />
  <xi:include href="applications/sec-more-markov.ptx" />
  <xi:include href="applications/sec-pagerank.ptx" />
</chapter>
